{"id": "EUVD-2026-94323", "enisaUuid": "4fbc1b70-bb7a-3c2f-ac66-7e158a84b8ee", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: fix use-after-free of retransmit_skb_hint in tcp_send_synack()\n\nWhen tcp_send_synack() replaces the cloned SYN skb at the head of the\nretransmit queue with a copy, it frees the original with\ntcp_rtx_queue_unlink_and_free() and only repairs tp->highest_sack.\ntp->retransmit_skb_hint keeps pointing at the freed\nskbuff_fclone_cache object.\n\nThe dangling hint is read in tcp_verify_retransmit_hint() and used as\nthe root of the rbtree walk in tcp_xmit_retransmit_queue().  An\nunprivileged TFO client (sendmsg(MSG_FASTOPEN)) can arm the hint with\nan attacker-supplied ICMP fragmentation-needed message, after which a\nsimultaneous open frees the armed SYN skb:\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in tcp_mark_skb_lost (net/ipv4/tcp_input.c:1316)\n  Read of size 4 at addr ffff88800604d928 by task swapper/1/0\n  Call Trace:\n   tcp_mark_skb_lost (net/ipv4/tcp_input.c:1316)\n   tcp_simple_retransmit (net/ipv4/tcp_input.c:3158)\n   tcp_v4_err (net/ipv4/tcp_ipv4.c:587)\n\nSync the hint to the copy.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T13:01:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fad6d429651e748365e93ca54645accc212f0018", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c5b4da1f403a658c1c19766be2b426003ada419f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71d45049b0d631dfdbf3c65305f7fca676de023b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3ea71cb1408a013ed4e8a757b815f1a919324bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/631aa4cb45099f09e9385dd786bd291c6270bfc4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f87720c7e4bcab07c24888b3cf12bfe857bb90e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fe99bbeee5c5dbd3abc30721a8079ced59649d97"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2q84-vc4j-mp23", "CVE-2026-98374"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "112ff5dc-5342-30b8-ac93-0db2cb97d827", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c31b70c9968fe9c4194d1b5d06d07596a3b680de <c5b4da1f403a658c1c19766be2b426003ada419f"}, {"id": "15eff7a8-ed24-39e5-90b2-cd438ecdb0e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3e6a8ac3-ebb7-32df-b223-db131c5fbac0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c31b70c9968fe9c4194d1b5d06d07596a3b680de <e3ea71cb1408a013ed4e8a757b815f1a919324bd"}, {"id": "499d0fb8-7e05-39fb-9176-12b55609bf4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "6c8b90b6-f141-3e5d-8bec-ca68f4a1fbf7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c31b70c9968fe9c4194d1b5d06d07596a3b680de <631aa4cb45099f09e9385dd786bd291c6270bfc4"}, {"id": "7f8052a0-8e77-3f8c-afc9-66981ffc273a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "84059a93-fdf1-359f-9e03-e52b17af4ce0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "8d856657-5769-392e-8649-866af6deae65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "963cec23-5dbd-357e-b1ac-6b60c8dba5f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "a5e69807-c566-3a7b-b2fa-e7b7dbc58b2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a65d7d59-0803-3753-8628-d5a3d1432064", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}, {"id": "ad665bb3-f5f3-3e10-a7fe-3866a48b7364", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c31b70c9968fe9c4194d1b5d06d07596a3b680de <fe99bbeee5c5dbd3abc30721a8079ced59649d97"}, {"id": "c2a67665-db79-3017-aeda-a4428f775b94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"n